{"id":"four-four-one","name":"Four four one","chapter":"Tricks in three count / causal diagrams","kind":"pattern","page":23,"label":"22","jugglers":null,"objects":null,"timing":null,"pdf":"https://www.jugglingedge.com/pdf/highgate.pdf#page=23&view=FitH,613","passist":"https://alpha.passist.org/extended-siteswap/(2,4x)(4x,2)/(2,4x)(4x,2)","passist_candidate":"https://alpha.passist.org/extended-siteswap/(2,4x)(4x,2)/(2,4x)(4x,2)","notations":[{"type":"hg-siteswap-in-text","value":"441"},{"type":"hg-siteswap-in-text","value":"441"}],"derived":{"kind":"sync (per-juggler parts)","confidence":"low","matches_stated":null,"sync":{"per_juggler":{"A":"(2,4x)*","B":"(2,4x)*"},"drawn":{"A":"(2,4xp)(4x,2)(2,4x)(4xp,2)(2,4x)(4x,2)(2,4xp)(4x,2)(2,4x)","B":"(2,4xp)(6,2)(2,6p)(2x,0)(2,4x)(4x,2)(2,4xp)(4x,2)(2,4x)"}}},"body":[{"t":"p","h":"What happens if Ben wants to combine a heff with an early double?"},{"t":"d","i":0},{"t":"p","h":"When you add the heff and the early double to the causal diagram, you have to remove the lines for the two single self throws, but there&#x27;s still a problem. There&#x27;s one left hand beat in Ben&#x27;s pattern that has no arrow pointing to it, and one right hand beat that has no arrow pointing from it. We can fix this by drawing an arrow from the right hand beat to the left hand beat!"},{"t":"d","i":1},{"t":"p","h":"As this arrow points to the left of the diagram, we have to draw the arrow head. An arrow pointing back one beat represents a zip or a hand-across. So this arrow shows Ben handing a club from his right to his left hand. In order to receive this club in his left hand he has to throw the club that he&#x27;s already holding in that hand. So the right hand zip causes the left hand pass one beat earlier! Don&#x27;t worry if you don&#x27;t understand the last two sentences, all you need to know is that an arrow pointing one beat back is a zip."},{"t":"p","h":"This is known as Tarim&#x27;s 441 in three count. The full combination trick for Ben is: pass heff double zip self self. Anne&#x27;s pattern is unchanged apart from having to catch a double."},{"t":"p","h":"It&#x27;s also possible to throw an early double followed by a heff to give another 441 trick."},{"t":"d","i":2},{"t":"p","h":"Ben throws: pass self double heff zip self. Once again Anne&#x27;s pattern is unchanged apart from having to catch a double."}],"drawings":[{"file":"p23-3.png","kind":"causal diagram","reading":{"rows":[{"juggler":"A","name":"Anne","offset":0.0,"tempo":1.0,"beats":[{"t":0.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":1.0,"hand":"L"},{"t":2.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":3.0,"hand":"L"},{"t":4.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":5.0,"hand":"L"},{"t":6.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":7.0,"hand":"L"},{"t":8.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":9.0,"hand":"L"},{"t":10.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":11.0,"hand":"L"},{"t":12.0,"hand":"R"}]},{"juggler":"B","name":"Ben","offset":0.0,"tempo":1.0,"beats":[{"t":0.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":1.0,"hand":"L"},{"t":2.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":3.0,"hand":"L"},{"t":4.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":5.0,"hand":"L","grey":true},{"t":6.0,"hand":"R","grey":true},{"t":7.0,"hand":"L"},{"t":8.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":9.0,"hand":"L"},{"t":10.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":11.0,"hand":"L"},{"t":12.0,"hand":"R"}]}],"arrows":[{"from":[0,0.0,"R"],"to":[1,1.0,"L"]},{"from":[0,1.0,"L"],"to":[0,2.0,"R"]},{"from":[0,2.0,"R"],"to":[0,3.0,"L"]},{"from":[0,3.0,"L"],"to":[1,4.0,"R"]},{"from":[0,4.0,"R"],"to":[0,5.0,"L"]},{"from":[0,5.0,"L"],"to":[0,6.0,"R"]},{"from":[0,6.0,"R"],"to":[1,7.0,"L"]},{"from":[0,7.0,"L"],"to":[0,8.0,"R"]},{"from":[0,8.0,"R"],"to":[0,9.0,"L"]},{"from":[0,9.0,"L"],"to":[1,10.0,"R"]},{"from":[0,10.0,"R"],"to":[0,11.0,"L"]},{"from":[0,11.0,"L"],"to":[0,12.0,"R"]},{"from":[1,0.0,"R"],"to":[0,1.0,"L"]},{"from":[1,1.0,"L"],"to":[1,2.0,"R"]},{"from":[1,2.0,"R"],"to":[1,3.0,"L"]},{"from":[1,3.0,"L"],"to":[0,4.0,"R"]},{"from":[1,7.0,"L"],"to":[1,8.0,"R"]},{"from":[1,8.0,"R"],"to":[1,9.0,"L"]},{"from":[1,9.0,"L"],"to":[0,10.0,"R"]},{"from":[1,10.0,"R"],"to":[1,11.0,"L"]},{"from":[1,11.0,"L"],"to":[1,12.0,"R"]},{"from":[1,5.0,"L"],"t